WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.320
- [Coach] I lost my job.

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.520
I lost my coaching career.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.353
I mean,

00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:04.186
I lost everything.

00:00:04.186 --> 00:00:05.019
I mean,

00:00:05.019 --> 00:00:05.852
it was brutal.

00:00:05.852 --> 00:00:08.292
(catchy music)

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.540
[Announcer] There are things
I regret doing on camera.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.373
3,

00:00:17.373 --> 00:00:18.206
2,

00:00:18.206 --> 00:00:19.039
1.

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:26.200
- [Isha] I was really drunk in a bar

00:00:27.775 --> 00:00:30.810
and I confronted one of
our other cast members

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:33.090
about what his political
views might have been.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.605
And I think,

00:00:34.605 --> 00:00:37.080
maybe that's the one thing I feel

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.180
like I probably shouldn't have done.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.399
- I mean,

00:00:40.399 --> 00:00:41.330
sometimes we try

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.410
and say something and it just
doesn't come out perfectly.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.970
If it made somebody feel bad,

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.050
somebody I care about

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.130
or I feel bad about that,

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:47.963
for sure.

00:00:47.963 --> 00:00:50.610
- I just kind of hate looking
back at it and not feeling

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.340
like I was my own person

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.990
and aligning with somebody who

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:55.830
in the real world,

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.810
I never would've aligned with.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:58.914
- [Michael] Yeah.

00:00:58.914 --> 00:01:00.720
I said a lot of out-of-pocket
jokes on my show

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.256
and a lot of people were mad.

00:01:02.256 --> 00:01:03.990
I don't regret saying any of it,

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.143
'cause at the time I thought
it was kind of funny.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:08.941
It's who I am.

00:01:08.941 --> 00:01:11.070
I say dumb (censored)

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.415
- [Coach] I mean,

00:01:12.415 --> 00:01:13.248
did I do stupid things?

00:01:13.248 --> 00:01:14.081
Maybe.

00:01:14.081 --> 00:01:16.093
Did I say things that
were out of character?

00:01:16.093 --> 00:01:17.256
Maybe.

00:01:17.256 --> 00:01:18.330
I think for me,

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.370
regret would be a wasted emotion

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:22.260
because through your mistakes,

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:23.250
that's when you really grow.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:24.360
When we're doing all the right things,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.200
we don't ever grow.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.580
And so looking back

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:27.413
on what I could've,

00:01:27.413 --> 00:01:28.246
would've,

00:01:28.246 --> 00:01:30.004
should've done to me,

00:01:30.004 --> 00:01:31.440
doesn't make sense.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:32.865
I just use the mistakes

00:01:32.865 --> 00:01:35.763
and try to channel that
into making a better person.

00:01:36.786 --> 00:01:39.288
- [Announcer] The
producers try to portray me

00:01:39.288 --> 00:01:40.242
as someone I'm not.

00:01:40.242 --> 00:01:41.417
3,

00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:42.250
2,

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:43.083
1.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:53.100
- [Holly] I had such
paranoia and such anxiety,

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.465
because of things that certain producers

00:01:55.465 --> 00:01:58.320
were trying to get me to say on the show.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.930
They tried to get me to body
shame one of my castmates,

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:03.090
they tried to get me to
say some kind of mean,

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.040
catty things that were
very out of character

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.139
for me to the point where,

00:02:06.139 --> 00:02:07.950
one of the producers who I liked

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:10.680
and felt safe with jokingly
called me "Regina George",

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.286
because I would always
express to him how I hated

00:02:13.286 --> 00:02:16.980
that the other producers tried
to get me to be a mean girl.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:17.813
- When I got back,

00:02:17.813 --> 00:02:18.646
everybody was like,

00:02:18.646 --> 00:02:19.479
"Did you cheat?"

00:02:19.479 --> 00:02:20.670
"Did you lie?"

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:21.900
"Were you a villain?"

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:22.733
I was like,

00:02:22.733 --> 00:02:23.880
I'm gonna be a hero.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.140
And my father said it best

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.060
about midway through the
first season I was on.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.362
And he was like,

00:02:28.362 --> 00:02:29.195
well I turned off the TV,

00:02:29.195 --> 00:02:30.090
midway through the show.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.913
They're making a (censored)
out on my son on national TV.

00:02:31.913 --> 00:02:33.240
I lost my job.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.667
I lost my coaching career.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:35.500
I mean,

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.333
I lost everything.

00:02:36.333 --> 00:02:37.483
I got hate mail every day.

00:02:37.483 --> 00:02:38.316
I mean,

00:02:38.316 --> 00:02:39.330
it was brutal.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:40.560
So on the one side,

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.679
I felt like the heroic parts that I did

00:02:43.679 --> 00:02:45.990
were not put in there.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:46.823
However,

00:02:46.823 --> 00:02:49.170
if I skipped to this other side

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:53.850
I also feel like they
film us 24 hours a day.

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:54.683
I'm pretty eclectic.

00:02:54.683 --> 00:02:56.910
They picked up on that straight away.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.680
And so they were like,

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.540
we're gonna gonna just
expand the boundaries.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:01.530
So when I watch myself,

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:02.892
I'm like,

00:03:02.892 --> 00:03:03.821
that's not me.

00:03:03.821 --> 00:03:04.800
But then on the other time I'm like,

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:05.633
oh wait,

00:03:05.633 --> 00:03:06.466
that is me.

00:03:06.466 --> 00:03:08.703
- I wish I was different
than what the show shows.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:11.820
It was me.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:12.653
Unfortunately,

00:03:12.653 --> 00:03:15.287
a lot of people didn't like it - me,

00:03:15.287 --> 00:03:16.743
and that's okay.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.458
- [Announcer] I always wanted
to be on a reality TV show.

00:03:21.458 --> 00:03:22.504
3,

00:03:22.504 --> 00:03:23.460
2,

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:24.573
1.

00:03:28.005 --> 00:03:28.980
(Michael laughs)

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.730
- [Michael] Why am I not surprised?

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.350
- [James] I won most likely
to be on a reality show

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.459
in high school.

00:03:35.459 --> 00:03:38.880
It's been part of my being. (laughs)

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.100
I grew up watching Survivor

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:41.933
Big Brother,

00:03:41.933 --> 00:03:42.780
and The Amazing Race.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.940
Those three shows had such a huge impact

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:45.870
on my life growing up,

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.760
just because it was an opportunity

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.570
for me to see other gay
members of the LGBT community

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.790
be a voice for someone
like me from the Midwest,

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:56.400
who'd never really had that to look up to.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.780
- When people said to me,

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:58.613
man, I applied

00:03:58.613 --> 00:04:00.060
for this show for 10 years in a row.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.147
I'm like,

00:04:01.147 --> 00:04:02.614
man, you guys gotta get a life.

00:04:02.614 --> 00:04:05.531
(everyone laughs)

00:04:06.541 --> 00:04:07.500
No but I mean,

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.790
to apply a couple of times,

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.170
but over and over,

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:12.175
I never watched it.

00:04:12.175 --> 00:04:15.573
- [Announcer] I got along
with the other contestants.

00:04:16.453 --> 00:04:17.286
3,

00:04:17.286 --> 00:04:18.119
2,

00:04:18.119 --> 00:04:18.952
1.

00:04:25.079 --> 00:04:25.912
- [Coach] I didn't go out

00:04:25.912 --> 00:04:28.800
and specifically seek
adversity with my castmates.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:31.726
But at the same time I was
trying to push the envelope

00:04:31.726 --> 00:04:34.380
and do things differently
than they had ever been.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.640
It was really surprising though,

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:36.570
when you're watching

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:38.190
you get really nervous before the episode,

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:40.140
'cause you have no idea
what they're gonna grab

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:41.190
for the final edit.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:42.030
So when people would say,

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.307
yeah, coach is such a (censored).

00:04:44.307 --> 00:04:45.361
I mean,

00:04:45.361 --> 00:04:46.885
I think that was hard.

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:48.050
But on the flip side,

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.320
I made some really strong bonds.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:50.995
- I met my girlfriend on the show,

00:04:50.995 --> 00:04:53.610
so we get along pretty well

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:54.964
but all the other cast,

00:04:54.964 --> 00:04:57.204
we're just so different.

00:04:57.204 --> 00:05:00.223
There's just no scenario
that we would be hanging out,

00:05:00.223 --> 00:05:03.180
other than just being
forced to live together.

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:04.440
- [Holly] I mean I can
get along with everybody.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.600
It doesn't mean I have to
like them or respect them.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.430
And we get a lot of flack for associating

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:09.263
with certain people.

00:05:09.263 --> 00:05:10.096
And it's like,

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.628
what do you do want me to
go against this person?

00:05:12.628 --> 00:05:13.461
He's in power.

00:05:14.298 --> 00:05:15.330
I have to pretend to like him.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:16.560
This is not real life,

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:17.393
people.

00:05:17.393 --> 00:05:18.570
- We have a group chat on WhatsApp

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.760
with all 22 of us still to this day.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.560
And over half of them were able to come

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.360
to our wedding in December.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.280
I recognize what we had was very special,

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.593
but I also know that
it's not for everyone.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.481
- [Announcer] Viewers would be
surprised about what happened

00:05:32.481 --> 00:05:34.442
behind the scenes.

00:05:34.442 --> 00:05:35.275
3,

00:05:35.275 --> 00:05:36.108
2,

00:05:36.108 --> 00:05:36.941
1.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:41.700
- The game is real,

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.350
the competition's real.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:46.500
Every aspect of that side of it is real.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:47.796
But,

00:05:47.796 --> 00:05:50.247
every single conversation I have with

00:05:50.247 --> 00:05:52.080
and somebody who loves the show,

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.670
no matter how long they've watched it,

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:54.600
they always say like,

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.710
oh my gosh that's so surprising.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.023
I know that.

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.484
So clearly it is.

00:05:58.484 --> 00:05:59.442
And for us,

00:05:59.442 --> 00:06:00.275
even in the house week one,

00:06:00.275 --> 00:06:01.221
we were talking

00:06:01.221 --> 00:06:02.054
we're like,

00:06:02.054 --> 00:06:03.480
wait, there's no screen in the diary room?

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:05.160
Mind blowing small things.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:05.993
So yeah,

00:06:05.993 --> 00:06:07.221
they're surprised.

00:06:07.221 --> 00:06:10.620
I'm not gonna say their life
is gonna be rocked or changed.

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:11.453
- At the end of the day,

00:06:11.453 --> 00:06:12.720
it's a TV show.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.750
So you just see what's
in front of the camera.

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:18.066
But if the camera were to just turn

00:06:18.066 --> 00:06:18.976
around once,

00:06:18.976 --> 00:06:20.190
there's a whole crew.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:22.399
- If you were to tell someone like,

00:06:22.399 --> 00:06:23.232
oh this happened

00:06:23.232 --> 00:06:24.325
behind the scenes,

00:06:24.325 --> 00:06:25.814
but they had watched the show.

00:06:25.814 --> 00:06:26.647
They wouldn't be like, (gasps)

00:06:26.647 --> 00:06:27.480
they'd be like,

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.313
oh that makes sense.

00:06:28.313 --> 00:06:29.146
That person seemed like that

00:06:29.146 --> 00:06:30.242
they would do that.

00:06:30.242 --> 00:06:31.075
- [Michael] Yeah.

00:06:31.075 --> 00:06:31.908
- You know what I mean?

00:06:31.908 --> 00:06:32.741
- Behind the scenes,

00:06:32.741 --> 00:06:33.960
there's no behind the scenes.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.664
They are always

00:06:35.664 --> 00:06:36.497
they're adamant

00:06:36.497 --> 00:06:37.330
if we don't get it the first time,

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.330
we will not ask you to
recreate a situation.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.031
I never saw the host in Tribal say,

00:06:42.031 --> 00:06:43.320
okay, hold on a second.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.790
Let me ask that different.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:45.623
It's all one take.

00:06:45.623 --> 00:06:47.130
And when you're not on

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.270
not filming something

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:49.950
you're on absolute strict lockdown.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:51.000
You can't talk to anybody.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.440
If the cameras aren't rolling,

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:53.640
you don't talk to anybody else.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:54.547
And if you do talk to somebody else,

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:56.370
somebody's gonna jump your (censored)

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:57.960
and they're gonna be like, shut up.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:06:58.793
You shut up.

00:06:58.793 --> 00:06:59.626
Look that way.

00:06:59.626 --> 00:07:00.459
Look that way.

00:07:00.459 --> 00:07:02.880
And you're basically persona non grata

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:05.880
when the cameras aren't rolling.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:09.990
- [Announcer] Reality TV
accurately represents reality.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:10.950
3,

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:11.910
2,

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:12.743
1.

00:07:16.664 --> 00:07:17.937
- [Holly] No, I would say yeah,

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:18.922
- [Kyland] Accurately.

00:07:18.922 --> 00:07:22.320
Reality TV demonstrates the extremes.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:24.600
The world just isn't binary.

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.040
It doesn't operate in extremes.

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.020
It shows you some things that are real,

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:31.200
but it doesn't accurately
reflect the world

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.910
because you know

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.190
that's - when people sit down and talk

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:37.129
they usually find out
they have more in common

00:07:37.129 --> 00:07:38.370
than they thought.

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:39.903
- [Coach] It's interesting

00:07:39.903 --> 00:07:41.284
because fans really think it's real life.

00:07:41.284 --> 00:07:42.980
- [Kyland] They do.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.220
- [Coach] It's crazy.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:45.531
I mean,

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:46.534
somebody can say,

00:07:46.534 --> 00:07:48.890
yeah Johnny Depp is captain Jack Sparrow

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:50.220
and they can be less convinced

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:52.470
of that than looking at
us and saying these guys,

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.699
that's exactly how they are in real life.

00:07:54.699 --> 00:07:56.532
It's a

00:07:56.532 --> 00:07:57.967
TV show.

00:07:57.967 --> 00:08:00.510
Most TV shows are not real.

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:02.910
- People really do have
a hard time realizing

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:04.980
that this is not a real world situation.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:07.200
These scenarios you would never be in.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:08.550
And the high stress

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:09.960
and the lack of sleep.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:10.793
I mean,

00:08:10.793 --> 00:08:12.447
at least I did not sleep for 99 days.

00:08:12.447 --> 00:08:15.840
It is not any normal situation
that you would put yourself

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:16.673
in.

00:08:16.673 --> 00:08:17.697
However,

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:19.320
the emotions and the experiences

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:20.280
that happen are very,

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:22.248
very raw and very,

00:08:22.248 --> 00:08:23.257
very real.

00:08:23.257 --> 00:08:26.580
And I think anyone in
those scenarios would have

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:27.870
those raw real emotions.

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:29.430
And that's another thing that is hard.

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:31.877
I think for viewers to realize
when they're so critical

00:08:31.877 --> 00:08:35.305
of how we responded to certain things,

00:08:35.305 --> 00:08:36.138
it's like

00:08:36.138 --> 00:08:36.971
well,

00:08:36.971 --> 00:08:38.418
it take my shoes,

00:08:38.418 --> 00:08:40.650
please wear them and see how you would do.

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:43.920
- Sometimes what you say
or an emotion you display,

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:46.710
might be used in a different
context to fit a narrative

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:47.543
that wants to

00:08:47.543 --> 00:08:50.013
be told for the overall show.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:54.300
So I'm glad I didn't
focus on that accurately

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.340
that I am focusing on
the accurately display

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:57.747
of reality 'cause it doesn't,

00:08:57.747 --> 00:08:58.980
it's not very accurate.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.380
- I think it depends what your reality is.

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:03.380
So if you're put on a show like Survivor,

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:04.484
well that's a weird,

00:09:04.484 --> 00:09:07.290
forced reality that that's not,

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:09.660
I mean that's clearly
not like what reality is,

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:12.342
but if you're on My 600-Lb Life,

00:09:12.342 --> 00:09:14.444
you're 600 pounds.

00:09:14.444 --> 00:09:15.690
That's their life.

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:16.860
That's real to them.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.054
- Yeah.

00:09:18.054 --> 00:09:20.100
I wish that viewers would realize
the separation of reality,

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.350
but also give us a little more grace

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:24.333
in the flawed human moments.

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.458
- [Announcer] Reality TV is an

00:09:27.458 --> 00:09:29.490
important form of entertainment.

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:30.570
3,

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:31.680
2,

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:32.513
1.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:37.450
